Restore backups
******************************************************************
./scripts/restore_db.sh backups/event_mgmt2026-03-30_20-25-31.sql.gz
1. run this using git bash or power shell.
Will the DATE in the restore command change?
✅ YES — and this is IMPORTANT

The date is part of the backup filename, not the command itself.

Your backups look like this:

employee_mgmt_2026-02-06.sql.gz
employee_mgmt_2026-02-07.sql.gz
employee_mgmt_2026-02-08.sql.gz


So when restoring, you choose which backup file you want:

./scripts/restore_db.sh backups/employee_mgmt_2026-02-08.sql.gz

| Situation                      | Restore? |
| ------------------------------ | -------- |
| First deploy (fresh DB)        | ❌        |
| Normal update                  | ❌        |
| Server restart                 | ❌        |
| Data lost                      | ✅        |
| Moving to new PC/server        | ✅        |
| After `docker compose down -v` | ✅        |





